  "limitations": [
    "SystemControl retains a pointer. Manager reinitialization and finalization can change manager+8, but no all-order lifetime or runtime stale-pointer conclusion is made.",
    "Immediate [Rn,#0x48] word-load/store scan covers the named code window. Computed aliases, arbitrary indirect branches and other tasks or cores are outside this scan.",
    "The observed FwPartition pointer reaches Emmc lock/unlock, not a partition table write. The proven +0x10 word stores target the separately allocated mutex. Power branches observed here update subsystem flags or clock state. The broader effects of external subsystem calls and hardware remain bounded.",
    "FwPartition byte+0x10 nonzero producer and an actual CPU writer for slot2 record+4 remain unresolved. Prior whole-table read can receive external sector bytes, and actual media values remain unknown.",
    "Genuine angr C is unmodified. The guard C outputs omit tail unlocks and the state dispatcher C omits external tail calls. ARM instructions and synthetic checks preserve those transfers."
  ]
